import{_ as n,o as a,c as t,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 819 | Transcended Ones and Planes | Plane Classification and Differentiated Governance","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 819 | Transcended Ones and Planes | Plane Classification and Differentiated Governance","no":819,"module":4,"tags":["Transcended One","Plane","Plane Classification","Differentiated Governance","Myriad-Rank Republicanism"],"related":["80-Plane Theory and Classification","30-Five Symbiotic-Civilization Typology Overview","17-Plane-Sovereign Strong-One Standards"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0819_模块4-超脱者与位面-位面分类与差异化治理.md","filePath":"en/0819_模块4-超脱者与位面-位面分类与差异化治理.md"}'),o={name:"en/0819_模块4-超脱者与位面-位面分类与差异化治理.md"};function r(s,e,l,d,c,p){return a(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="entry-819-transcended-ones-and-planes-plane-classification-and-differentiated-governance" tabindex="-1">Entry 819 | Transcended Ones and Planes | Plane Classification and Differentiated Governance <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-819-transcended-ones-and-planes-plane-classification-and-differentiated-governance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 819 | Transcended Ones and Planes | Plane Classification and Differentiated Governance&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 80, 30, 17</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-a-thousand-planes-have-a-thousand-ways-of-living-—-the-transcended-one-may-not-measure-all-planes-with-one-ruler" tabindex="-1">Introduction: a thousand planes have a thousand ways of living — the transcended one may not measure all planes with one ruler <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-a-thousand-planes-have-a-thousand-ways-of-living-—-the-transcended-one-may-not-measure-all-planes-with-one-ruler" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: a thousand planes have a thousand ways of living — the transcended one may not measure all planes with one ruler&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old system&#39;s handling of planes is very rough: the strong one arrives at a plane, transforms it by his own standard — this plane&#39;s cultivation system must be like mine, laws must follow mine, civilization must follow the route I planned. This &quot;great unification&quot; thinking turns a rich cosmos into monotonous copy-paste. Heng Yuan Zhou rejects this practice. In the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s orthodox framework, <strong>planes are not uniform templates, but homes with their own character.</strong> The transcended one&#39;s governance is not &quot;transform all planes into the same,&quot; but &quot;respect each plane&#39;s differentiated development within a unified framework.&quot;</p><p>Six top-level axioms in this entry centrally embody the republican axiom of Myriad Races: Myriad Ranks&#39; diversity itself is the cosmos&#39; wealth, not to be smoothed out. The anti-predation axiom requires differentiated governance not become &quot;unequal treatment, discriminating against the weak&quot;; the collective ascension axiom requires differentiated governance&#39;s ultimate goal still be pushing overall uplift; the causal self-discipline axiom requires cross-plane governance not disturb each plane&#39;s natural development trajectory; the law-first axiom requires differentiated governance&#39;s classification standard itself be a law-level definition, not casually classified by the transcended one&#39;s personal preference.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>This article focuses: how the transcended one conducts differentiated governance of different plane types.</p><h2 id="i-planes-four-basic-types" tabindex="-1">I. Planes&#39; Four Basic Types <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-planes-four-basic-types" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Planes&#39; Four Basic Types&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Per Plane Theory and Classification (Document 80) and Five Symbiotic-Civilization Typology Overview (Document 30), planes in Heng Yuan Zhou by development stage and civilizational maturity divide into four basic types:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Plane Type</th><th>Development Stage</th><th>Civilizational State</th><th>Transcended-One Governance Focus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nascent plane</td><td>Newly opened or newly discovered</td><td>No civilization or civilization in embryo</td><td>Provide basic protection, do not interfere with natural development</td></tr><tr><td>Growing plane</td><td>Civilization initially established</td><td>Cultivation system forming</td><td>Guide direction, provide public infrastructure</td></tr><tr><td>Mature plane</td><td>Civilization highly developed</td><td>Cultivation system complete, Myriad-Rank republicanism running well</td><td>Maintain stability, promote innovation</td></tr><tr><td>Declining plane</td><td>Civilization showing regression signs</td><td>Law drift, energy-cycle deterioration</td><td>Emergency intervention, ecological restoration, prevent historical regression</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Four types are not fixed labels — a plane&#39;s type changes with civilizational development. The transcended one&#39;s governance strategy must adjust accordingly: a nascent plane grows into a growing plane; a growing plane matures into a mature plane; a mature plane in trouble may also degrade into a declining plane.</p><h2 id="ii-differentiated-governance-s-four-principles" tabindex="-1">II. Differentiated Governance&#39;s Four Principles <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-differentiated-governance-s-four-principles" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Differentiated Governance&#39;s Four Principles&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one&#39;s differentiated governance of different plane types follows four principles:</p><ol><li><strong>Minimal-intervention principle</strong>: for nascent and growing planes, the transcended one intervenes as little as possible — only strikes when civilization faces an existential-level crisis; daily development lets the plane go its own way. Over-intervention is like pulling up seedlings to help them grow.</li><li><strong>Infrastructure principle</strong>: for growing planes, the transcended one&#39;s main work is providing public infrastructure — anchor access, cultivation-system opening, public energy-pool construction. When infrastructure is in place, plane civilization will grow by itself.</li><li><strong>Innovation-guarantee principle</strong>: for mature planes, the transcended one&#39;s work shifts from &quot;construction&quot; to &quot;guarantee&quot; — guaranteeing civilizational innovation is not locked by old paths; guaranteeing new cultivation systems and new civilizational experiments have trial-and-error room.</li><li><strong>Emergency-repair principle</strong>: for declining planes, the transcended one must quickly intervene — law-stability repair, energy-cycle reconstruction, civilizational-correction engineering. A declining plane without timely repair may collapse in a short time.</li></ol><p>Four principles&#39; common logic: <strong>what the plane needs, the transcended one provides; what the plane does not need, the transcended one does not over-manage.</strong> Governance is not &quot;how I want to do it,&quot; but &quot;what the plane needs me to do.&quot;</p><h2 id="iii-differentiated-governance-and-myriad-races-full-coverage-s-unity" tabindex="-1">III. Differentiated Governance and Myriad-Races-Full-Coverage&#39;s Unity <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-differentiated-governance-and-myriad-races-full-coverage-s-unity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Differentiated Governance and Myriad-Races-Full-Coverage&#39;s Unity&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Some worry: will differentiated governance become &quot;unequal treatment&quot; — strong planes get more care, weak planes are neglected? Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s design is exactly the opposite:</p><ul><li><strong>Resource allocation linked to need</strong>: anchor resources, energy quotas, and technical support a plane receives are allocated per its development stage&#39;s actual needs — nascent planes most need basic protection, so basic-protection resources take priority; mature planes most need innovation guarantee, so trial-and-error room takes priority. Not allocated by strength, but by need.</li><li><strong>Development rights absolutely equal</strong>: no matter the plane type, the evolutionary rights of Myriad Ranks on the plane are absolutely equal. A cultivator on a nascent plane and a cultivator on a mature plane have exactly the same qualification to access Alaya Network, right to use public cultivation resources, and voting right in Myriad-Rank Republican deliberation.</li><li><strong>Progress channels open</strong>: a plane&#39;s type is not a lifelong label — any plane may through civilizational development go from nascent to mature. The transcended one&#39;s governance work is ensuring this progress channel is always open.</li></ul><p>Differentiated governance ≠ discrimination. It is &quot;on-demand service,&quot; not &quot;strength-based allocation.&quot;</p><h2 id="iv-the-transcended-one-s-plane-inspection-system" tabindex="-1">IV. The Transcended One&#39;s Plane-Inspection System <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-transcended-one-s-plane-inspection-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The Transcended One&#39;s Plane-Inspection System&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Differentiated governance requires the transcended one periodically inspect each plane, understanding the plane&#39;s real state — he may not sit in an office judging by data, but must perceive on the ground. Inspection system:</p><ul><li><strong>Inspection frequency</strong>: mature planes inspected once per standard cycle; growing planes once per half-cycle; nascent and declining planes once per quarter;</li><li><strong>Inspection content</strong>: law stability, energy-cycle state, civilizational-development trend, Myriad Ranks&#39; living conditions, anchor-network operating state;</li><li><strong>Inspection method</strong>: the transcended one blends into plane life as an ordinary cultivator, not revealing identity — only in real daily life may he see the real effect of plane governance;</li><li><strong>Inspection report</strong>: after inspection, submit a written report recording the plane&#39;s state, discovered problems, and suggested adjustment plans.</li></ul><p>The inspection system ensures: the transcended one&#39;s governance decisions are not based on abstract data, but on personal experience of the plane&#39;s real state. He is not a manager watching fire from across the shore, but a guardian walking into the fire.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: differentiated governance ensures resources are invested where each plane most needs them, avoiding waste caused by &quot;one-size-fits-all&quot; resource misallocation</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: need-based allocation + equal development rights institutionally prevent the transcended one from favoring strong planes and sacrificing weak planes</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo strong ones transform all planes by their own standard, uniform; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s transcended one respects each plane&#39;s differentiated development, each with character</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Myriad-Rank cultivators on all four plane types are covered by governance; no matter plane size, strength, newness, treated equally</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: plane-classification standards, four governance principles, and the inspection system are all publicly queryable; each plane may supervise whether governance is fair</p></li><li><p>Terminology alignment: the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm is this batch&#39;s standard realm appellation; the transcended one&#39;s civilizational weight dynamically adjusts with post performance; Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision monitors operation compliance throughout; the Myriad-Origin two-way cycle ensures energy and knowledge circulate perpetually among Myriad Ranks; exercise of law-anchor authority is strictly constrained by four-dimensional assessment and democratic procedure.</p></li><li><p><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Plane classification and differentiated governance is the republican axiom of Myriad Races&#39; refined fulfillment at the plane dimension. A thousand planes have a thousand ways of living; the transcended one does not try to turn them into one way. He manages nascent planes lightly, paves roads for growing planes, guarantees mature planes, and rush-repairs declining planes — governance strategy follows the plane&#39;s actual needs, not his personal preference. When every plane may develop at its own pace and with its own character, the multiverse truly becomes Myriad Ranks&#39; home — not a home carved from one mold, but a home of a hundred flowers blooming.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/80-位面理论与分类.html">Entry 80 · Plane Theory and Classification</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/30-五种共生文明分型总览.html">Entry 30 · Five Symbiotic-Civilization Typology Overview</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/17-位面至高强者标准.html">Entry 17 · Plane-Sovereign Strong-One Standards</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/816_模块4-超脱者与位面-总论.html">Entry 816 · Transcended Ones and Planes Overview</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const g=n(o,[["render",r]]);export{h as __pageData,g as default};
